    "problem_statement": "### Description\n\nThere seems to be an issue with the deterministic behavior of pickling dynamic classes using `cloudpickle`. The pickling process does not consistently produce the same output for classes with similar structures, which can lead to unexpected results when attempting to serialize and deserialize these classes.\n\n### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport cloudpickle\nimport subprocess\n\ndef check_deterministic_pickle(dump1, dump2):\n    assert dump1 == dump2, \"Pickle outputs are not deterministic\"\n\ndef subprocess_worker(protocol):\n    # Simulate a subprocess worker for testing\n    return subprocess.Popen(['python'], stdin=subprocess.PIPE, stdout=subprocess.PIPE)\n\nwith subprocess_worker(protocol=3) as w:\n    class A:\n        \"\"\"Simple class definition\"\"\"\n        pass\n    A_dump = w.run(cloudpickle.dumps, A)\n    check_deterministic_pickle(A_dump, cloudpickle.dumps(A))\n\n    class A:\n        name = 'A'\n        __doc__ = 'Updated class definition'\n    A_dump = w.run(cloudpickle.dumps, A)\n    check_deterministic_pickle(A_dump, cloudpickle.dumps(A))\n\n    class A:\n        def __init__(self):\n            \"\"\"Class definition with explicit __init__\"\"\"\n            pass\n    A_dump = w.run(cloudpickle.dumps, A)\n    check_deterministic_pickle(A_dump, cloudpickle.dumps(A))\n```\n\n### Expected Results\n\nThe serialized output of the class `A` should be consistent across different instances of pickling, ensuring that the pickled data is identical for the same class structure.\n\n### Actual Results\n\nThe pickled data for class `A` is not consistent, leading to different outputs for what should be identical class definitions. This inconsistency can cause issues when relying on deterministic behavior for serialization and deserialization processes.\n\n### Versions\n\n```\nSystem:\n    python: 3.10.15\n    cloudpickle: 2.0.0\n    platform: Linux\n```"
